{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y_obs`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y_obs` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The parameter `f_predict` has exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before it is used in the model likelihood. Other data variables are context inputs used only as predictors, indices, constants, or transformed-data configuration.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N_predict;
  array[N_predict] real x_predict;

  int<lower=1> N_obs;
  array[N_obs] real y_obs;
  array[N_obs] int<lower=1, upper=N_predict> observed_idx;

  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N_predict, N_predict] cov =   gp_exp_quad_cov(x_predict, alpha, rho)
                                     + diag_matrix(rep_vector(1e-10, N_predict));
  matrix[N_predict, N_predict] L_cov = cholesky_decompose(cov);
}

parameters {
  vector[N_predict] f_predict;
}

model {
  f_predict ~ multi_normal_cholesky(rep_vector(0, N_predict), L_cov);
  y_obs ~ normal(f_predict[observed_idx], sigma);
}

generated quantities {
  array[N_predict] real y_predict = normal_rng(f_predict, sigma);
}

